    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch06-14: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.69";
    dc:description "Large invasion datasets support broad tests of the island-versus-mainland implication. They test a proxy for local competitive adaptation, not perfection itself or its exclusive production by selection.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Compare establishment, displacement, abundance, and performance of introduced versus endemic species across islands and continents while controlling for propagule pressure and environment. Systematic competitive replacement supports the prediction; endemic superiority under matched conditions opposes it.";
